{
  "description": "HELD-OUT TEST set (v6) for the bridge-fact retrieval milestone. 20 BRIDGE questions: each needs an entity chunk AND a rule/data/code chunk that does not name the entity (require_all), the failure shape verified on v5 (entity chunk ranks 1-2, bridge chunk 9-25). 12 single-chunk lookups are regression controls. Written BEFORE the section-path embedding prefix existed and never used for tuning. By the AI assistant, who KNEW the planned approach while writing (not independent); questions use player phrasing, and none of v5's five failures is reused. PRE-REGISTERED primary metric: full-coverage recall@5 on bridge questions, baseline vs prefix, paired sign test. Secondary: lookup MRR@10 (regressions) and end-to-end correct (qa_v6.json).",
  "kinds": {
    "bridge_rule": "entity chunk + a general rule chunk that never names the entity",
    "bridge_data": "entity chunk + data/waves.json (counts, no shared vocabulary)",
    "bridge_code": "entity chunk + a code chunk (tower.gd) whose formula applies to it",
    "lookup": "one chunk states the answer; a regression control"
  },
